      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we use the tangent addition formula. Specifically, we use the identity:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - \\theta) = \\frac{1 - \\tan \\theta}{1 + \\tan \\theta}\n\\]\n\nLet \\(\\theta = 20^\\circ\\). Then we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan(45^\\circ - 20^\\circ) = \\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nRewriting the right-hand side in terms of \\(\\tan 20^\\circ\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nNow, let \\(x = \\tan 20^\\circ\\). Then \\(\\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x}\\). Substituting these into the original expression, we have:\n\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 + x)(1 + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x})\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n1 + \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\frac{(1 + x) + (1 - x)}{1 + x} = \\frac{2}{1 + x}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n(1 + x) \\cdot \\frac{2}{1 + x} = 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified value of \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
