    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We first use the double angle formula for tangent to simplify the expression. Recall that $\\tan(2\\theta) = \\frac{2\\tan(\\theta)}{1 - \\tan^2(\\theta)}$.\n\nApplying this formula to $\\tan 45^\\circ = \\tan(2 \\cdot 20^\\circ) = \\frac{2\\tan 20^\\circ}{1 - \\tan^2 20^\\circ}$, we can rewrite the expression as:\n$(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\frac{1 - \\tan^2 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan^2 20^\\circ})$\n\nNow let's simplify the second term:\n$\\frac{1 + \\tan^2 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan^2 20^\\circ} + \\tan 20^\\circ = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ$\n\nSubstituting this back into the expression, we get:\n$(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\frac{1 - \\tan^2 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan^2 20^\\circ}) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan^2 20^\\circ)$\n\n$= (2 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan^2 20^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ - \\tan^3 20^\\circ)$\n\nNow, let's use the fact that $\\tan 45^\\circ = 1$. This means $\\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} = \\tan 25^\\circ$, or $\\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ}$.\n\nSubstituting this into the expression, we get the simplified answer:\n$(2 + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan^2 25^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ - \\tan^3 25^\\circ) = (2 + \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} + \\tan^2 25^\\circ + \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} - \\frac{\\tan^{3/2} 20^\\circ}{\\tan 20^\\circ})$\n\nSince $\\tan 45^\\circ = 1$, we can rewrite this as:\n$(2 + \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} + \\tan^2 25^\\circ + \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} - \\tan^{3/2} 25^\\circ)$\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n$2 + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} + \\tan^2 25^\\circ$\n\nFinally, we can simplify this expression further using the identity $\\tan(45^\\circ) = 1$:\n$2 + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\tan 20^\\circ} + \\tan^2 25^\\circ = 2 + 2 \\cdot \\tan 20^\\circ$\n\nTherefore, the simplified value of $(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)$ is $\\boxed{4}$.",
